  "title": "CHAPTER 10: HISTORY OF ODISHA – MODERN PERIOD & FREEDOM STRUGGLE",
  "order": 11,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "rzql65s",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10.1 British Rule in Odisha"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The British East India Company defeated the Bhonsle Marathas and captured Odisha in 1803 (Treaty of Deogaon). Initially Odisha was part of Bengal Presidency. In 1912 it was separated from Bengal and became part of Bihar &amp; Orissa Province.",
      "id": "ujwr8rl"
    },
    {
      "id": "oo2i96g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10.2 Paika Rebellion (1817)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Paika Rebellion (also called Paika Bidroha) of 1817 is considered by many historians as the FIRST WAR OF INDEPENDENCE against the British in India, predating the 1857 revolt by 40 years. The Paikas were the peasant militia of the Gajapati kings of Odisha.",
      "id": "3c7d6kt"
    },
    {
      "id": "obetmoi",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
