    {
      "id": "w2ncver",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10.4 Veer Surendra Sai"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Veer Surendra Sai (1809–1884) is Odisha's most celebrated freedom fighter. He was the heir to the throne of Sambalpur but the British did not recognize his claim. He fought against the British for over 30 years. He was finally captured and transported to Asirgarh Fort (MP) in 1864, where he died in 1884. He is called 'Veer' (brave) of Odisha.",
      "id": "9kt9vs5"
    },
    {
      "id": "2so4ajd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10.5 Odisha as Separate Province"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "After a long struggle led by Utkalmani Gopabandhu Das and others, the Utkal Sammilani was established in 1903 to demand a separate province for Odia-speaking people. On 1 April 1936, the Province of Odisha was carved out as a separate linguistic province – the first in India.",
      "id": "xyfk6zg"
    },
    {
