    {
      "id": "7nhmg8o",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "10.7 Formation of Modern Odisha"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Odisha became a state on 1 April 1936 under the Government of India Act, 1935. After independence, Odisha became a part of the Indian Union on 15 August 1947. The state was renamed from 'Orissa' to 'Odisha' officially on 4 November 2011 by an Act of Parliament, and the Odia language name was also updated.",
      "id": "i7t2sxa"
    }
  ],
  "enriched": false
